{
  "$comment": [
    "Netiflux bundled themes. Loaded into Terminal.Gui's ConfigurationManager at startup.",
    "To add your own theme, copy one of these blocks into ~/.tui/config.json (or",
    "%USERPROFILE%\\.tui\\config.json) under a top-level \"Themes\" array. Anything you put",
    "there overrides what ships here, so you can also retune a single scheme of a built-in",
    "theme without copying the whole thing.",
    "",
    "Scheme roles used by Netiflux:",
    "  Base        - window chrome and general surfaces",
    "  Sidebar     - the views/feeds/categories rail",
    "  EntryUnread - unread rows in the entry list (should read as 'bright / demands action')",
    "  EntryRead   - already-read rows (should recede)",
    "  EntrySaved  - rows pushed to the bookmark service (distinct accent, the triage payoff)",
    "  Reader      - the article body",
    "  ReaderMeta  - byline and separators inside the reader",
    "  Banner      - the title bar strip",
    "  StatusGood / StatusBad - transient toasts"
  ],

